  "checks": [
    "A separate platform administrator is created through the real users API and receives an explicit BUILDING_ADMIN membership; no factor or session proof is written directly by this case.",
    "The UI login returns enrollment-required with empty operational memberships. The required gate is visible, navigation is absent and the protected building GET denies with MFA_ENROLLMENT_REQUIRED.",
    "Real UI enrollment and TOTP confirmation return ten unique recovery codes; Close and Escape cannot dismiss the held ceremony, while its original UI bearer already reports satisfied at the server.",
    "No page-originated non-auth API request is observed before the response event for a GET/auth/me initiated after acknowledgment is armed. That response body is then separately checked for the same identity, satisfied state and explicit membership.",
    "After acknowledgment the page requests buildings, navigation becomes visible, saved codes leave the DOM, and direct reads using the original UI bearer prove the correct building plus units:manage and teams:manage capabilities.",
    "The required settings UI offers no disable button. A direct real HTTP disable attempt with the same proven UI bearer denies403/MFA_REQUIRED and preserves the enabled factor, ten unused recovery codes and satisfied session state."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Exactly one independent required-MFA administrator case is accepted; prior three-case browser and renderer results remain separate evidence and are not added here.",
    "Only the legacy flag-based ADMIN with one explicit local BUILDING_ADMIN membership is exercised. This does not cover support users, RBAC-only administrator grants, all authority combinations or new family verification-required recovery.",
    "The network oracle is page.on(request), excluding separate APIRequestContext setup/assertion calls. Its boundary is the200 response event/headers for the post-arming acknowledgment GET/me, with body identity checked afterward; it is not internal provider-mount instrumentation or universal request/parsing linearization.",
    "One Chromium worker and zero retries; no Firefox/WebKit matrix, Android, iOS, device, Codegen, full webapp or load acceptance.",
    "This increment executes E2E types and one-case listing. The prior V4 building type result is reused only because all product sources and its config match exactly; no new building type execution is claimed.",
    "A QA-only ESM startup entrypoint invokes the same application, restricted-role checks and event bus, then binds127.0.0.1; the product server.ts is preserved.",
    "The frontend consumer is freshly built in production mode; API and fixture execute with NODE_ENV=test on a disposable UUID database.",
    "Visual review means the final screenshot and three sampled video frames, not watching every frame or asserting exhaustive UX coverage.",
    "The raw MFA video remains private because the scenario displays ephemeral factor/recovery material. No public video is eligible from this run; publication of a reviewed final screenshot is a separate root action.",
    "The2048MiB memory requirement is a phase/startup guard, including the observation after API/preview startup. Heartbeats during the browser run are measurements, not a continuous2048MiB acceptance threshold.",
    "No performance conclusion, production readiness, deployment, migration publication, commit or push is performed by this verifier."
  ],
